      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0737",
      "reading_order": 854,
      "section": "Oil requirements based on temperature",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 143.99594000000002,
        "t": 708.64184,
        "r": 545.72598,
        "b": 673.40184
      },
      "content": "For the majority of  operating conditions, bearing temperatures run between 120°F (49°C) and 180°F (82°C), and you can use an oil of  ISO viscosity grade 68 at 100°F (38°C). If  temperatures exceed 180°F (82°C), refer to the table for temperature requirements."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "tbl_0042",
      "reading_order": 855,
      "section": "Oil requirements based on temperature",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 143.4268798828125,
        "t": 673.5096817016602,
        "r": 558.8899536132812,
        "b": 596.1769409179688
      },
      "markdown": "| Temperature                                    | Oil requirement                                                                                                                                                                    |\n|------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Bearing temperatures exceed 180°F (82°C)       | Use ISO viscosity grade 100 with bearing-frame cooling or finned-tube oil cooler. The finned-tube oil cooler is standard with the HT 3196 model and optional for all other models. |\n| Pumped-fluid temperatures exceed 350°F (177°C) | Use synthetic lubrication.                                                                                                                                                         |"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0738",
      "reading_order": 856,
      "section": "Acceptable oil for lubricating bearings",
